Package: sdrnapred
Title: Positional Base-Preference Scoring for Chemically Modified Self-Delivering siRNAs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Paper2Agent", "Reimplementation", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "noreply@example.com")
Description: An independent reimplementation of the linear regression-based
    positional base-preference algorithm for predicting the efficacy of
    cholesterol-conjugated, chemically modified, self-delivering siRNAs
    (sdRNAs), described by Shmushkovich, Monopoli and colleagues in Nucleic
    Acids Research (2018) <doi:10.1093/nar/gky745>. The package builds a
    per-position, per-base weight matrix from a training set of 50-nucleotide
    target regions and their measured efficacies, scores new target sequences
    against that matrix, and evaluates predictions with positive predictive
    power versus sensitivity curves and ROC analysis. The 356-compound training
    set from the paper's Supplementary Table 1 is bundled. This package is not
    the authors' own code, which was never released; see the README for a
    point-by-point account of where the published description is ambiguous and
    how closely the reimplementation reproduces the paper's reported benchmarks.
